  "term": "ophthalmoplegia",
  "definition": "Ophthalmoplegia is paralysis of one or more muscles that move the eye. It results from problems in the eye muscles themselves or in the tissues, tendons, nerve supply, or neuromuscular junctions that support their movement.",
